itle><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1996</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>2738</fpage><lpage>2746</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8874335</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="display-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Kaplan-Meier survival estimates. <bold>(a) </bold>Patients undergoing mastectomy alone and those receiving adjuvant chemotherapy or radiotherapy, or both. <bold>(b) </bold>By ethnic group. Chemo, chemotherapy; RT, radiotherapy.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bcr1658-1"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Hazard rates for death in ethnically Chinese breast cancer patients. <bold>(a) </bold>Mastectomy alone. <bold>(b) </bold>Adjuvant chemotherapy without radiotherapy. <bold>(c) </bold>Radiotherapy without chemotherapy. <bold>(d) </bold>Both modalities. <bold>(e) </bold>Local therapy only. <bold>(f) </bold>Systemic therapy. Note the different scale used for the hazard in panel d. Chemo, chemotherapy; RT, radiotherapy.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bcr1658-2"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Smoothed hazard for death in ethnically Chinese breast cancer patients. <bold>(a) </bold>Mastectomy alone. <bold>(b) </bold>Adjuvant chemotherapy without radiotherapy. <bold>(c) </bold>Radiotherapy without chemotherapy. <bold>(d) </bold>Both modalities. <bold>(e) </bold>Local therapy only. <bold>(f) </bold>Systemic therapy. Note that the tail of the curve was removed because of the small number of available data. Chemo, chemotherapy; RT, radiotherapy.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bcr1658-3"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Smoothed hazard for death in ethnically Chinese breast cancer patients having mastectomy alone. <bold>(a) </bold>Lymph node negative. <bold>(b) </bold>Lymph node positive. <bold>(c) </bold>Pathological T1. <bold>(d) </bold>Pathological T2 or T3. <bold>(e) </bold>Premenopausal. <bold>(f) </bold>Postmenopausal patients. <bold>(g) </bold>Well to moderately differentiated. <bold>(h) </bold>Poorly differentiated. <bold>(i) </bold>ER positive. <bold>(j) </bold>ER negative. Note that the tail of the curve was removed because of the small number of available data. ER, oestrogen receptor.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bcr1658-4"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F5"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Smoothed hazard for death in ethnically Malay breast cancer patients. <bold>(a) </bold>Mastectomy alone. <bold>(b) </bold>Adjuvant chemotherapy without radiotherapy. <bold>(c) </bold>Radiotherapy without chemotherapy. <bold>(d) </bold>Both modalities. <bold>(e) </bold>Local therapy only. <bold>(f) </bold>Systemic therapy. Note that the tail of the curve was removed because of the small number of available data. Chemo, chemotherapy; RT, radiotherapy.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bcr1658-5"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F6"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Smoothed hazard for death in ethnically Indian breast cancer patients. <bold>(a) </bold>Mastectomy alone. <bold>(b) </bold>Adjuvant chemotherapy without radiotherapy. <bold>(c) </bold>Radiotherapy without chemotherapy. <bold>(d) </bold>Both modalities. <bold>(e) </bold>Local therapy only. <bold>(f) </bold>Systemic therapy. Note that the tail of the curve was removed because of the small number of available data. Chemo, chemotherapy; RT, radiotherapy.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bcr1658-6"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristics in patients treated with mastectomy by type of adjuvant therapy received</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left">Characteristic</td><td align="center" colspan="4">Adjuvant therapy</td><td align="left">Total (<italic>n </italic>= 2105)</td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan="4"><hr></hr></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="left"